1
00:00:00,05 --> 00:00:02,03
- [Instructor] In a typical React application,

2
00:00:02,03 --> 00:00:05,01
data is passed top-down, from parents to child,

3
00:00:05,01 --> 00:00:06,03
via the props.

4
00:00:06,03 --> 00:00:09,00
This needs to be done manually, from top to bottom,

5
00:00:09,00 --> 00:00:11,03
by going through every component's level,

6
00:00:11,03 --> 00:00:13,09
which can be very tedious and difficult to maintain.

7
00:00:13,09 --> 00:00:17,00
This works very well for small and basic applications.

8
00:00:17,00 --> 00:00:19,00
But imagine you have much bigger applications

9
00:00:19,00 --> 00:00:20,05
with multiple levels.

10
00:00:20,05 --> 00:00:22,04
It can become very challenging.

11
00:00:22,04 --> 00:00:24,06
And so the more complex is the application,

12
00:00:24,06 --> 00:00:27,07
the more complex is the communications between components

13
00:00:27,07 --> 00:00:29,09
and the more complex it is to share the state

14
00:00:29,09 --> 00:00:31,05
across the application.

15
00:00:31,05 --> 00:00:33,08
The solution is the Context API.

16
00:00:33,08 --> 00:00:36,09
That is a way to share values without having to explicitly

17
00:00:36,09 --> 00:00:39,02
and manually pass the data from the parents

18
00:00:39,02 --> 00:00:41,01
to the child components.

19
00:00:41,01 --> 00:00:44,06
So why use a context object and the Context API?

20
00:00:44,06 --> 00:00:47,02
First, it provides a way to manage the application state

21
00:00:47,02 --> 00:00:49,04
in a single, centralized location.

22
00:00:49,04 --> 00:00:52,03
And it helps to avoid the common pitfall of props drilling.

23
00:00:52,03 --> 00:00:55,03
So you don't need to pass the data manually and explicitly

24
00:00:55,03 --> 00:00:57,06
by going through every component's level.

25
00:00:57,06 --> 00:01:00,04
You just need to define a global state, which is shared

26
00:01:00,04 --> 00:01:01,09
with several components.

27
00:01:01,09 --> 00:01:05,01
In one single location, the state is easier to manage

28
00:01:05,01 --> 00:01:07,03
and easier to synchronize across the components

29
00:01:07,03 --> 00:01:09,00
of the application.

30
00:01:09,00 --> 00:01:10,03
So let's see it in action.

31
00:01:10,03 --> 00:01:11,08
We're going to refactor the application

32
00:01:11,08 --> 00:01:14,04
and see what we can do with the Context API.

33
00:01:14,04 --> 00:01:18,00
Coming next, we're going to create a new context object.

